tickets.body:
## Outcome and ownership
Verify the land mission and settlement paths that generated-world inputs change: scene selection from the generated battle-index map and location mapping (MMR-42), spawn and return positions, generated settlements/relationships and generated troops. Entry/return fidelity for one land battle and one settlement location is already proven by MMR-60. Stock in-mission mechanics on unchanged stock scenes (keep-fight variants, sally-out/relief, prison break, wall-breach and gate AI traversal, hideout night lighting, arena) are not retested.

Representative set, run from designated test saves of world A (use B where A lacks a case; mark a case absent from both worlds as absent, never passed):
- one field battle for each distinct battle terrain present, including one substituted terrain (for example Mountain to Steppe), and one crossing/bridge encounter;
- town entry with one interior (tavern or hall) and a notable or merchant conversation; castle entry; village entry;
- one hideout clear;
- one siege assault with deployment;
- one party defeat leading to capture and escape, and one retreat.

Use only accepted asset mappings; generated settlements and relationships remain the active world. Check character/gear visuals for each culture present, encyclopedia names and location menus. Attach logs/captures per scenario; automatic XML validation is not proof of player-facing missions. The official spawn debug tooling is an extra diagnostic only.
